x86_64-linux  cxx1 names a static local `_ZL7countedi.calls` where Itanium spells it _ZZL7countediE5calls - docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "A static local keeps its own name in the object file" - and its guard `.guard` where clang writes _ZGVZ...; the same objects under two names, as static-local-constructor.nonames records. And clang names __cxa_guard_abort and _Unwind_Resume for the landing pad that releases the guard if an initialiser throws, which cxx1 does not emit - docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "A static local's guard is not released if its constructor throws".
x86_64-windows  the same static locals and guards in cxx1's own spelling, where clang writes ?calls@?1??counted@@YAHH@Z@4HA and ?$TSS0@?1??counted@@YAHH@Z@4HA.
arm64-darwin  the same static local name for the constant one, __ZL8constantv.c against __ZZL8constantvE1c, and ___cxa_guard_abort and __Unwind_Resume for the pad cxx1 does not emit.
